                <pb facs="0674" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 103.93/69: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-28T13:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1919—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 29—2:47 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2989. For Polk. Your 3604, August 9, 7 p.m. Please notify press associations and
                    newspaper correspondents that transmission of their news matter by wireless from
                    Paris to America will be discontinued, the last filings to be made in Paris on
                    August 30th; the news report and editorial summary heretofore transmitted by the
                    New York office of the mission will be continued by the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
